  "name": "Find and qualify Google Maps leads with AI into Google Sheets",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ab12a4b2-2e91-52c7-bcee-cf558e30a331",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -560,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 940,
        "content": "## Find and qualify Google Maps leads with AI, into Google Sheets\n\n**Who's it for:** agencies, freelancers and B2B sales teams who prospect local businesses and want the list sorted by how well each business matches their offer, without wiring an LLM themselves.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Reads your searches from a Google Sheet: a search term, a city and your ideal customer in one sentence. Searches marked done are skipped.\n2. Runs the **Google Maps Scraper API** actor on Apify for each search. Every place comes with phone, website, rating and reviews count, plus AI verdicts: fit with your ideal customer (0 to 1), digital maturity, online booking expected but missing, independent or chain, size, price tier.\n3. Attaches each place to its search and appends the places above your fit threshold to a *Leads* sheet, best first (all of them when a search has no ideal customer).\n4. Marks each search as done, with the number of places scanned and leads found.\n\n**How to set up**\n- Create a sheet with two tabs, *Searches* and *Leads*, with the columns of the yellow note.\n- Connect Google Sheets in the three Sheets nodes and pick the right tab in each.\n- Add your Apify API token as an Apify credential (install the verified Apify node if needed).\n- Adjust *Settings*: minimum fit, places per search, language.\n\n**Requirements:** an Apify account. No OpenAI or other AI key: the verdicts are part of the actor.\n\n**Cost:** $0.50 per 1,000 places plus $1 per 1,000 places qualified, paid to Apify. 50 places with verdicts cost about $0.08.\n\n**Customize:** reword the ideal customer per search (\"independent restaurant without online booking\", \"dental practice with fewer than 10 people\"), raise `min_fit`, or add your own yes/no questions with `customQuestions` in the *Find and qualify places* node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a30d183b-7abe-538b-adb8-14ca1c27118d",
      "name": "Sheet columns",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        60,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "### Sheet columns\n\n**Searches** tab (you fill the first three):\n`search` \u00b7 `location` \u00b7 `ideal_customer` \u00b7 `status` \u00b7 `leads_found` \u00b7 `places_scanned`\n\n**Leads** tab (filled by the workflow):\n`search` \u00b7 `name` \u00b7 `fit` \u00b7 `category` \u00b7 `phone` \u00b7 `website` \u00b7 `rating` \u00b7 `reviews` \u00b7 `digital_maturity` \u00b7 `booking_tool` \u00b7 `booking_missing` \u00b7 `ownership` \u00b7 `size` \u00b7 `price_tier` \u00b7 `listing_gaps` \u00b7 `address` \u00b7 `maps_url`\n\nRows whose `status` is `done` are skipped, so you can add searches over time and run it again. A search that finds no place stays pending."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
